WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:06.150
In A Clash of Kings, Daenerys Targaryen meets “three seekers” – Pyat Pree, Xaro Xhoan

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.440
Daxos, and Quaithe – who are kinda like
the three wise men of the Bible – they come

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.130
after a miraculous birth beneath a special
star, and give gifts to a possible prophesied

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:20.069
saviour – but anyway – Pyat Pree is a
douchebag warlock guy, Xaro Xhoan Daxos is

00:00:20.069 --> 00:00:25.479
a douchebag “merchant prince” guy, and
Quaithe is… a mystery. She wears a red mask,

00:00:25.479 --> 00:00:30.220
and calls herself “Quaithe of the Shadow”. Like Melisandre, she says she’s a shadowbinder

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.010
from Asshai. A shadowbinder seems to be someone
who uses shadow magic – like Mel does to

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:39.920
kill Renly and Cortnay Penrose – and Asshai
is a city at the edge of the known world,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.910
steeped in darkness and magic and mystery, much like Quaithe herself – beyond her

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:49.510
name and where she’s from, we know nothing
about this woman. Yet she repeatedly appears

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:54.559
to Dany, offering cryptic advice. What’s
her deal?

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:59.189
In Qarth, Quaithe tells Dany to “Beware
… Of all” who might want to take her dragons,

00:00:59.189 --> 00:01:04.629
which as Jorah says, is good advice. Later, she says magic is becoming more powerful in

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:08.259
the world of ice and fire, which is something
we’ve heard before, but she implies

00:01:08.259 --> 00:01:12.790
that it’s happening because of the birth
of Dany’s dragons. Then Quaithe tells Dany

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:18.030
to leave Qarth. Dany asks where she should
go, and Quaithe says this: “To go north,

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:22.979
you must journey south. To reach the west,
you must go east. To go forward you must go

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:28.240
back, and to touch the light you must pass
beneath the shadow”. At first Dany thinks

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.270
this means Quaithe wants her to go to Asshai, which is, after all, “Easternmost and

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:36.100
southernmost of the great cities of the known
world”, so she asks “What is there in

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.829
Asshai that I will not find in Qarth?”,
and Quaithe just says “Truth”. It’s

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:45.469
probably possible for Dany to go to Asshai – it's about as close to Qarth as Meereen is. Some

00:01:45.469 --> 00:01:49.820
suggest Dany might pass through Asshai, go
all the way east, and approach Westeros from

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:54.070
the west. But there’s good reason not to
believe that Dany goes to Asshai – George

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:58.880
R. R. Martin has said that “[We will see
Asshai] Only in flashback and memory, if at

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:03.539
all”. Further, it seems really silly to
have such a cryptic riddle solved immediately

00:02:03.539 --> 00:02:08.750
after we hear it. Right? So it seems unlikely
that Quaithe means for Dany to go to Asshai.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:13.940
But she means something important, ’cause
in the next book, in Slaver’s Bay, Quaithe

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:18.800
appears to Dany again, seemingly in a dream,
and repeats the go back to go forward thing.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.060
In Dance, Quaithe appears a third time, and
this is where she speaks the most. Dany asks

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:26.940
Quaithe if she’s dreaming, and Quaithe says
“no”, but she also says that she’s not

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:32.500
actually there, and that only Dany can see
her. She then says “The glass candles are

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.160
burning”. This may explain how Quaithe
keeps appearing to Dany when she sleeps – glass

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:41.580
candles are magical Valyrian artefacts that
allow communication over long distances, kinda

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:47.160
like palantiri in Lord of the Rings, or just,
like, uh, phones. But glass candles, according

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.360
to Marwyn the Mage, allow you to “enter
a man’s dreams and give him visions”, which

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.830
sounds like what’s happening to Dany. And
it’s plausible that Quaithe might have a

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:58.820
glass candle, it’s not like they’re super-rare
– the maesters of the Citadel have a bunch,

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.580
the Targaryens of Aemon’s day seem to
have had some, and someone called Urrathon

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:07.790
Night-Walker has some, in Qarth, where Quaithe presumably still is. So it looks like Quaithe

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:11.050
is using a glass candle to communicate with
Dany.

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:17.150
That’s one puzzle solved, but Quaithe gives
us more. She says “Soon comes the pale mare,

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:23.030
and after her the others. Kraken and dark
flame, lion and griffin, the sun’s son and

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:28.620
the mummer’s dragon. Trust none of them.
Remember the Undying. Beware the perfumed

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:33.010
seneschal”. This is basically a list of
everything and everyone Dany has to deal with.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:37.290
“[T]he pale mare” is the disease that
ravages Slaver’s Bay, “the others” probably

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.680
the Yunkai’i. The “kraken”’s Victarion
and maybe Euron, the “dark flame” is

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.870
Moqorro, the “lion” Tyrion, the “griffin”
Jon Connington, “the sun’s son” Quentyn

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.840
Martell. “[T]he mummer’s dragon” is
probably Aegon, maybe hinting that he’s

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:54.250
no true Targaryen. And “the perfumed seneschal”
could be a bunch of stuff – maybe Reznak,

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:59.840
or Varys, or the ship Tyrion was on. Interestingly,
Quaithe mentions all these people, but not

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.410
Marwyn the Mage, who’s also coming for Dany.
And it just so happens that Marwyn uses a

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:09.640
glass candle – could he be in contact with
Quaithe? In any case, overall that stuff’s

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:13.750
pretty straightforward, and pretty accurate,
too, right? Dany notices that Quaithe predicts

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:18.259
“the pale mare” and Quentyn. But she
still doesn’t understand the go-back-to-go-forwards

00:04:18.259 --> 00:04:21.439
stuff.
Everything starts to make sense in Daenerys

00:04:21.439 --> 00:04:27.039
X, A Dance With Dragons. In this chapter,
Dany has a climactic kind of a vision quest

00:04:27.039 --> 00:04:32.039
at the edge of the Dothraki Sea. She eats
some funny berries, flies around on Drogon,

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:35.960
hallucinates – a lot like that scene in
Tenacious D, actually. But the point of this

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:40.939
for Dany is huge turning point in her character.
All through Dance, she tries to peacefully

00:04:40.939 --> 00:04:45.770
and diplomatically rule the city of Meereen
– she marries Hizdahr when she wants Daario,

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:50.229
she chains away her dragons when she wants
them free, she opens Daznak’s Pit, and allows

00:04:50.229 --> 00:04:54.629
Yunkish slavery, though she thinks it wrong,
all the while telling herself “If I look

00:04:54.629 --> 00:04:59.949
back I am lost”. That’s the mantra by
which she supresses the violent, uncompromising

00:04:59.949 --> 00:05:04.680
side of her personality, the Targaryen side.
And that’s how this chapter starts – she

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:09.060
tells herself her home is in Meereen, she
needs to bend before the whip, if she looks

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:14.919
back she is lost. But in this chapter, she
looks back. Quaithe appears, and says “Remember

00:05:14.919 --> 00:05:20.259
who you are … The dragons know. Do you?”
And her vision quest begins. A vision of Viserys

00:05:20.259 --> 00:05:24.629
reminds her of her Targaryen blood, the grass
reminds her that her dragons are her true

00:05:24.629 --> 00:05:29.810
children, a vision of Jorah reminds her that
Meereen is not her home, that her war is in

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:35.569
Westeros, he says “Remember your words”,
and Dany says “Fire and Blood”. So at

00:05:35.569 --> 00:05:40.469
the conclusion of this chapter, Daenerys says
“To go forward I must go back”. She flies

00:05:40.469 --> 00:05:45.590
off on Drogon, hunts and eats a horse, thinks
of Daario, and the chapter ends with the appearance

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:51.169
of a Dothraki khalasar. Dany is going back to
the Dothraki, back to the Targaryens, back

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:56.099
to “Fire and Blood”, and it all starts
with Quaithe. This is what Quaithe means when

00:05:56.099 --> 00:06:00.159
she says “To go forward you must go back”,
and the “go north [to go] south” and “east”

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:03.909
“to [go] west” stuff presumably means
the same thing, just a little more poetically.

00:06:03.909 --> 00:06:07.999
Admittedly, the bit saying “to touch the
light you must pass beneath the shadow”

00:06:07.999 --> 00:06:12.830
doesn’t really fit this interpretation very well.
The fact that Asshai is called Asshai-by-the-Shadow

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:16.870
does make it tempting to believe that this means
Dany will go to Asshai, but again, that seems

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:20.759
unlikely. So maybe the light and shadow stuff
will make more sense later. For now, we’ve got

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:25.639
a pretty good explanation of Quaithe’s prophecy.
“To go forward you must go back” refers

00:06:25.639 --> 00:06:31.620
to transformation of Dany’s character, a
return to violence and power and “Fire and

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.849
Blood”. Maybe she’ll lead a horde of Dothraki.
Maybe she’ll go burn her enemies in Slaver’s

00:06:35.849 --> 00:06:41.029
Bay. Maybe she’ll finally go to Westeros.
And maybe, with the loss of her gentler side,

00:06:41.029 --> 00:06:45.379
she’ll become a bit of a bad guy. This is
a big deal for Dany.

00:06:45.379 --> 00:06:48.620
But we still don’t know what’s
up with Quaithe. Who is she, and what does

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:54.610
she want? To answer these questions, let’s
“go back”, to the reign of King Aegon

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:59.559
IV Targaryen, more than a hundred years ago.
Known as “the Unworthy”, Aegon famously

00:06:59.559 --> 00:07:04.059
fathered lots of bastards, including the original
Daenerys Targaryen, after whom our Dany is

00:07:04.059 --> 00:07:08.889
named, but he also fathered someone called
Shiera Seastar, who according to one theory,

00:07:08.889 --> 00:07:13.449
is Quaithe. Now, for Quaithe to be Shiera,
she’d have to be more than a hundred years

00:07:13.449 --> 00:07:18.569
old, but funnily enough, Shiera Seastar’s
half-brother and lover was Brynden Rivers,

00:07:18.569 --> 00:07:24.539
a.k.a. Bloodraven, a.k.a. the three-eyed crow,
who Bran finds alive beyond the Wall, and

00:07:24.539 --> 00:07:29.550
who, like Quaithe, gives cryptic guidance
from afar. If Brynden extended his life, and

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:34.120
he was close with Shiera, maybe Shiera could
extend her life too. Of course, Quaithe is

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:38.069
not a tree-person, but The World of Ice and
Fire says Shiera’s mother was said to be

00:07:38.069 --> 00:07:42.169
a sorceress, and George R. R. Martin has said
Shiera “was reputed to practice

00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:46.430
the dark arts” – the same is said in The
Sworn Sword, specifically the she “bath[ed]

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:50.939
in blood to keep her beauty”. So it seems
totally possible that Shiera might magically

00:07:50.939 --> 00:07:55.849
extend her life. Further, there are strong
symbolic connections between her and Quaithe.

00:07:55.849 --> 00:08:00.949
Shiera is associated with stars – her mother
named her “Star of the Sea”. And in Daenerys

00:08:00.949 --> 00:08:06.449
X, in the Dothraki Sea, the stars whisper
Quaithe’s prophecy to Dany, and Dany sees

00:08:06.449 --> 00:08:11.430
Quaithe as a “mask … made of starlight”. Quaithe’s whole role in the story is symbolically

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:16.279
that of a sea star, a guiding light that “show[s]
[Dany] the way” when she’s “lost [on

00:08:16.279 --> 00:08:21.960
the Dothraki] sea”. Being Shiera may explain
Quaithe’s motivations – it makes sense

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:26.479
that a fellow Targaryen princess, or legitimised
bastard, whatever, would want to guide Dany

00:08:26.479 --> 00:08:31.509
back to her Targaryen roots, and return
to Westeros. Also, Shiera is said to have

00:08:31.509 --> 00:08:35.930
“spoke[n] a dozen tongues and surrounded
herself with ancient scrolls”. You’ve

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:39.770
gotta wonder – might some those ancient
scrolls have said something about a saviour

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:44.630
called Azor Ahai? That prophecy seems to come from Asshai, so maybe Shiera Seastar

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:49.400
went to Asshai for that reason, and she helps
Dany because, like Benerro and Aemon, she

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:54.120
thinks Dany is Azor Ahai. Or she might have
just gone to Asshai for general shadowbinding

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.810
black artsy stuff. Or maybe she’s never
even been to Asshai and she just says he has,

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:03.700
and wears a mask, and takes the name of Quaithe
to hide her identity – she was a famed beauty

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:07.590
in her day, maybe she doesn’t want to be
recognised. Maybe she had to leave Westeros

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:12.540
to hide her unnaturally long life. We could
speculate all day. The point is that there’s

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:17.080
fairly strong evidence that Quaithe may be
Shiera Seastar. It’s far from certain, some

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:21.150
things don’t fit – like, Shiera’s eyes
are different colours, and Dany doesn’t

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:26.100
notice that in Quaithe. But there are still
strong symbolic connections between the two,

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:31.540
and being Shiera may explain Quaithe’s motivations.
Whoever she is, Quaithe’s prophecy seems

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:37.210
to refer to a transformation in Daenerys’
character from peace and restraint to “fire

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:40.620
and blood”.
Thanks for watching. Let me know in the comments

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.080
whether you think Quaithe is Shiera Seastar,
and what topic you’d like to see next.

